  "userRequest": "ay esta funcionando la api y todo, podemso iniciar una nueva sesion",
  "description": "Shipped a broad round of El Carot work, all deployed to production (Vercel + Neon).\n\nReading actions: wired the Share button (Web Share API on mobile, copy-direct-link fallback on desktop with a toast) and the Save button (composes a phone wallpaper on a <canvas> — just the card art centred on a background sampled from the card's own frame colour, downloaded as PNG). Both guarded against hangs. Gallery cards already opened their reading.\n\nDesktop home redesign: a full-width row of face-up cards that drift slowly leftward as one (CSS marquee) while each sways at its own rhythm (negative-delay animations so they flow from the first frame); bigger cards; the three actions as a centred row of auto-width pills; a '♥ El Carot te ama ♥' sign-off pinned to the bottom; the welcome + wordmark title block nudged down; the whole card+buttons group vertically centred. Mobile keeps the fanned trio (buttons made shorter).\n\nNav & polish: EL CAROT wordmark centred and clickable-to-home on both mobile and desktop; a single aligned top-right cluster (language + Instagram + star) shared by the desktop nav and the home header, replacing the misaligned floating star on desktop; a menu context (lib/menu) so the star toggles the shared menu; favicon = the menu star on charcoal; About credit 'por @bastadanii' under the title; the reading card tilts + sways + casts a soft shadow; per-page desktop vertical centring (reading, message, about).\n\nAnalytics database: three new Prisma models on Neon Postgres. DailyCard stores one card per UTC day (chosen once, the SAME for everyone) — the reading page get-or-creates it, and a Vercel Cron (00:00 UTC, /api/cron/daily, CRON_SECRET-guarded) guarantees a row per day. Question logs every AI question (card, language, source, coarse geo). Visit logs one entry per session via a VisitTracker + /api/track. A password-protected /stats page (STATS_PASSWORD) shows the daily-card history (all days), questions, and visits-by-country. Geo is coarse Vercel IP data only (country / region / timezone) — never IP or precise location.\n\nInternationalisation: the middleware now defaults visitors from Spanish-speaking countries to Spanish (via Vercel's x-vercel-ip-country) before falling back to Accept-Language, so an Argentine visitor with an English browser gets Spanish.\n\nFooter: the 'CodeYam' credit now links to codeyam.com.\n\nAI model kept at claude-haiku-4-5 (cheapest) with the written-meaning fallback. Unit tests cover the pure share URL/text builders and the wallpaper card-rect math (26 green).",
